## Scenario context

As microservice architectures scale, a single outage in a core service can cascade across the entire system. Cell-Based Architecture mitigates this by partitioning the entire system into small, self-contained, independent units called cells. This guide outlines their routing mechanics and provides a custom Spring Cloud Gateway filter for cell-based traffic distribution.






